<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section xml:id="chapter6_for-statement">
    <title>The <c>for</c> Statement</title>

    <p>
        A <c>for</c> statement is useful when a loop has a clear starting value,
        continuation condition, and update step. The three parts appear in one
        line:
    </p>

    <program xml:id="program_for_count_to_100"
             language="cpp"
             interactive="yes">
        <code><![CDATA[
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    for (int count = 1; count <= 100; ++count) {
        std::cout << count << '\n';
    }

    return 0;
}
        ]]></code>
    </program>

    <table xml:id="table_for_statement_parts">
        <title>The parts of a <c>for</c> statement</title>
        <tabular>
            <row>
                <cell>Part</cell>
                <cell>Purpose</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
                <cell><c>int count = 1</c></cell>
                <cell>Initialize the loop variable.</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
                <cell><c>count &lt;= 100</c></cell>
                <cell>Continue while the condition is true.</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
                <cell><c>++count</c></cell>
                <cell>Update the loop variable after each iteration.</cell>
            </row>
        </tabular>
    </table>

    <p>
        The loop above prints the numbers from 1 through 100. The phrase
        <q>from 1 through 100</q> is a useful clue that a counted loop is needed.
    </p>

    <p>
        The update can move in different directions. For example, this loop
        counts down from 5 to 1:
    </p>

    <program xml:id="program_for_count_down"
             language="cpp">
        <code><![CDATA[
for (int count = 5; count >= 1; --count) {
    std::cout << count << '\n';
}
        ]]></code>
    </program>

    <p>
        A <c>for</c> loop can be rewritten as a <c>while</c> loop. The compact
        form is especially helpful when the initialization, condition, and
        update belong together.
    </p>
</section>
